    "body": "Closes #6393.\n\nDefining `__cinit__` twice in a cdef class compiled without any error, and the second definition silently replaced the first. Since a no-args `__cinit__` accepts any arguments, the result depended on the order of the two definitions.\n\nThis makes a second `__cinit__` an error, using the same \"already defined\" message as duplicate cdef methods. A subclass defining its own `__cinit__` is not affected.\n\nAdded `tests/errors/duplicate_cinit.pyx`. I ran it along with the other `__cinit__`/`__new__` tests and the full `errors` and `compile` suites locally, and they all pass.\n\nA duplicate `__dealloc__` is also accepted silently. I left it out to keep this small, but I'm happy to add it if you'd like.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
